cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or build on the PredRHEED framework, please cite it as below."
title: "PredRHEED: A Cascaded Deep-Learning Framework for In Situ RHEED Monitoring During ScAlN Molecular Beam Epitaxy"
type: software
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-11-06"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Walkerlino/PredRHEED"
abstract: >-
  PredRHEED is a cascaded deep-learning framework for in situ reflection
  high-energy electron diffraction (RHEED) monitoring during ScAlN molecular
  beam epitaxy. A memory-enhanced self-attention convolutional long short-term
  memory (MSAM-ConvLSTM) predictor forecasts future RHEED frames from 15 s of
  observed frames, and a CNN-Transformer hybrid classifier assigns the
  predicted frames to the streaky, transition, or spotty RHEED-pattern class.
  The evaluated end-to-end forecast horizon is 5 s.
keywords:
  - reflection high-energy electron diffraction
  - RHEED
  - molecular beam epitaxy
  - MBE
  - ScAlN
  - RHEED-pattern classification
  - future-frame prediction
  - cascaded deep-learning framework
